.TH "RECORD\-CREATE\-EDGE\.PY" "" "May 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-create\-edge\.py\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-create\-edge\.py\fR \fIEDGE_LABEL\fR \fIOUT_VERTEX_ID\fR \fIIN_VERTEX_ID\fR
.br
[\fIPROP_NAME\fR \fIPROP_VALUE\fR \|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-create\-edge\.py\fR creates a directed edge in a Gremlin graph database between two existing vertices\. The edge runs from the vertex identified by \fIOUT_VERTEX_ID\fR to the vertex identified by \fIIN_VERTEX_ID\fR and is labelled with \fIEDGE_LABEL\fR\. Zero or more edge properties may be supplied as additional positional argument pairs\.
.P
The script is intended for use with the Gremlin backend only\. If \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is set to any value other than \fBgremlin\fR the script writes an error to standard error and exits with a non\-zero status\.
.P
Vertices are located by their \fBname\fR property using a Gremlin \fBhas\fR traversal step\. Both \fIOUT_VERTEX_ID\fR and \fIIN_VERTEX_ID\fR must therefore correspond to the \fBname\fR property of existing vertices in the graph, not to their internal Gremlin vertex identifiers\.
.P
Within the RECORD workflow, \fBrecord\-create\-edge\.py\fR is called by \fBrecord\.sh\fR when inserting relationship records (such as \fBDEPENDENCY\fR, \fBUSES\fR, \fBPRODUCT\fR, and \fBIN_FILE\fR) into a Gremlin\-backed provenance store, in place of the SQL \fBINSERT\fR statements used by the relational backends\.
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIEDGE_LABEL\fR
The label to assign to the new edge (for example \fBDEPENDENCY\fR, \fBUSES\fR, or \fBPRODUCT\fR)\.
.TP
\fIOUT_VERTEX_ID\fR
The value of the \fBname\fR property of the source (outgoing) vertex\.
.TP
\fIIN_VERTEX_ID\fR
The value of the \fBname\fR property of the target (incoming) vertex\.
.TP
\fIPROP_NAME\fR \fIPROP_VALUE\fR
Zero or more property key\-value pairs to attach to the new edge\. Properties must be supplied in pairs; an odd number of additional arguments is an error\. Both keys and values are passed through \fBrecord\.gremlin_safe_string\fR before being embedded in the query\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This command takes no option flags\. All arguments are positional\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
fewer than three positional arguments are supplied;
.IP "\(bu" 4
the number of additional property arguments is odd;
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR is not \fBgremlin\fR;
.IP "\(bu" 4
the database connection fails; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
the Gremlin query raises an exception (for example, if either vertex does not exist)\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Must be set to \fBgremlin\fR\. The script exits immediately with an error if this variable is set to any other value\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_HOST\fR
WebSocket URL of the Gremlin server (default: \fBws://localhost:8182/gremlin\fR as set by \fBrecord\.py\fR)\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_GREMLIN_TIMEOUT\fR
Per\-query evaluation timeout in milliseconds (default: \fB30000\fR as set by \fBrecord\.py\fR)\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR
When set, enables verbose diagnostic output to standard error, including the full Gremlin query string and the parsed argument values\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
None\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Create a \fBDEPENDENCY\fR edge from application \fBapp_123\fR to application \fBapp_456\fR:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-create\-edge\.py DEPENDENCY app_123 app_456
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Create a \fBUSES\fR edge with an \fBoptionality\fR property:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-create\-edge\.py USES app_123 box_type_csv optionality always
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Create a \fBPRODUCT\fR edge with a \fBlocator\fR property:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-create\-edge\.py PRODUCT app_123 box_type_output locator stdout
.fi
.IP "" 0
