.SH "BUGS"
The usage message and the length check (\fBif len(sys\.argv) < 4\fR) are placed after the \fBreturn\fR statement of \fBparse_prop_pairs\fR and are therefore unreachable dead code\. Missing positional arguments will instead cause an \fBIndexError\fR when \fBsys\.argv[1]\fR, \fBsys\.argv[2]\fR, or \fBsys\.argv[3]\fR are accessed\.
.P
Vertices are located by their \fBname\fR property rather than by their Gremlin vertex ID\. If two vertices share the same \fBname\fR value the traversal may match more than one vertex, resulting in multiple edges being created silently\.
.P
The Gremlin query is constructed by simple string concatenation without parameterisation, which may produce malformed queries if \fIEDGE_LABEL\fR, \fIOUT_VERTEX_ID\fR, or \fIIN_VERTEX_ID\fR contain single\-quote characters, even though property values are passed through \fBgremlin_safe_string\fR\.
.P
The \fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR check is performed twice in \fB__main__\fR: once before parsing properties and once after\. The second check is redundant\.
